# THE TIDE TAKES THE REAPER (roadmap slice 1, step 4: force and one other way).
# It keeps the tide line and is far too heavy for the water it works beside
# (its FOUNDER way: MUD, WATER, RIVER, held 1.4 s). Roused, it follows the player
# into the shallows off its own shore, founders, and the land takes it. Over the
# shoulder, bare-handed: the plating does not matter to the sea.
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/reaper_tide.tour --seed=7 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --config=unharmed
coast calm
tap shoulder
await shoulder 3
# On the shallows off its shore, by name (`keeper_flats`: the nearest water its
# move reaches from its den, stood so its run at him ends in it), never by a
# heading, which a moved Reaper turned into a walk up the grass. Held out there,
# it comes on into the water and founders.
near keeper_flats
await sentinel 12
drive res://tests/fight/plate_reader.gd 60 sentinel_fallen lure
shot 01-the-tide-takes-it with shoulder,sentinel_fallen
wait 2.0
shot 02-foundered-off-its-own-shore with shoulder,sentinel_fallen
